From b4767f3316d0ff94db0850a005970d13016da572 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fmillion <47171880+fmillion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:47:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/45] drm/i915: Lakefield: USB-C DP alt mode on DDI D/E
 (experimental, i915.lkf_tc)

Lakefield's Type-C display ports are DDI D (TC1) and DDI E (TC2): ICL-style
FIA (DFLEXDPSP/CSSS/PMS), Gen11 DE TC hot-plug and ICL DDI_CLK_SEL/MG_PLL_ENABLE
clocking, but with the TGL Dekel PHY behind HIP_INDEX (0x168000/0x169000), as
programmed by the Lakefield GOP. The EHL-based description drives none of it.

With i915.lkf_tc=1:
- add a lakefield platform alias, DDI E to the port mask, D/E -> PHY D/E,
  TC1/TC2 and HPD_PORT_TC1/TC2;
- ICL TC clock hooks, Dekel signal levels/buffer translations, Dekel DP mode;
- a Lakefield DPLL manager: DPLL0/1, TBT PLL, TC PLL 1/2 on the Dekel PHY;
- do not index the (absent) PCH HPD table in the ICL TC live-status check.

Default off: without the parameter the existing behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
